<title>PERU: TABLE - Peru's H1 coffee output rises 10.6 percent.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Peru's H1 coffee output rises 10.6 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table outlines Peru's</p>
<p>latest coffee production and export figures released Friday:</p>
<p>		    PRODUCTION			 EXPORTS</p>
<p> June 1996	31,900 tonnes   May 1996     8,700 tonnes</p>
<p> June 1997	42,300 tonnes   May 1997     10,400 tonnes</p>
<p> Jan-June 1996  89,800 tonnes   Jan-May 1996 24,900 tonnes</p>
<p> Jan-June 1997  99,300 tonnes   Jan-May 1997 18,800 tonnes</p>
<p>NOTES:</p>
<p>- Source for statistics is Peru's Agriculture Ministry.</p>
<p>- The ministry releases coffee export figures a month later than production figures.</p>
<p>- Peru, whose principal coffee harvest is between April and November, is South America's number four producer after Brazil, Colombia and Ecuador, according to the government.</p>
<p>((-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
</text>
